From cbec7471d1b66006c688204833946cd17811851f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim <107831991+SyntaxError-PEBKAC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 19:54:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] ducksteps: resync stub installer CSS with ESR 153
 markup

Same staleness as the About dialog fix. Both stub installer stylesheets
were verbatim copies of ESR 140's official files, with nothing ducksteps
specific in either, and were never resynced.

This one was a functional mismatch, not just a layout drift. The markup
these style lives in browser/installer/windows/nsis/content/, outside
branding, so the build already ships 153's HTML. In 153 that HTML dropped
#text_column, #text_column_container, #header, #content, #installing and
#footer, leaving only #background, #label, #progress_background,
#progress_bar and #blurb. The 140 stylesheets spend most of their rules
on elements that no longer exist, and hide #blurb, which 153 actually
uses.

The 140 rules also set "body { color: black }", which #header and
#content inherited. Against our dark starfield bgstub.jpg that text was
effectively invisible, so these pages were likely already broken on 140.
It went unnoticed because we ship the full SEA installer
(dist/install/sea/firefox-VERSION.en-US.win64.installer.exe), not the
stub, so nothing built from these files reaches users.

Resynced against 153's official files, which use white text and a
centred layout. Note bgstub.jpg puts the duck in the left ~48% of the
frame, and 153 centres its text, so the composition is worth a look if
the stub installer is ever actually shipped. #background itself is styled
by the non-branding stub_common.css and is unaffected by this change.
